{"evidence":["Reviewed `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs`: save loading now goes through `SaveFile::from_value`, applies the ordered `MIGRATIONS` chain sequentially from `MIN_SUPPORTED_SCHEMA` to `SCHEMA_VERSION`, and enforces the registry/version-gap invariant with a compile-time assert.","Reviewed the version-parsing path in `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs`: oversized `schema_version` values are rejected via `u32::try_from` instead of silently truncating, future saves return `SchemaVersionTooNew`, and unsupported old saves return `SchemaVersionTooOld`.","Reviewed `crates/tank_api/src/handlers/save.rs`: the load endpoint now calls `SaveFile::from_value` directly, removing the redundant `Value -> String -> Value` round-trip without changing the validation/migration path.","Reviewed `crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs`: coverage includes v2->current migration, legacy saves missing `stability_tracker`, future-version rejection, too-old rejection, zero-version rejection, and save/load determinism.","Verified the workspace with `cargo test`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and `cargo fmt --check`; all passed."],"findings_or_gaps":[],"follow_up_or_amendments":[],"outcome":"approved"}